--- body ---
## Context

`data/reference/vietnam_thermal_v1.csv` is frozen at commit `85a0e6c7` for
Exp1–3 (see `data/reference/PROVENANCE.md`). The Exp2 FP audit surfaced 17
`clean_name` collisions and mixed romanization. Line-by-line adjudication
(units_included in hand) re-diagnosed the picture: only 1 true duplicate
(`Duyen Hai 2`, romanization), 2 raw-name key collisions (`Dong Nai Formosa`,
`Ha Tinh Formosa` — distinct base/extension assets sharing one name string),
and 14 distinct-plant pairs that collide only after the cleaner's
`^lng`/`^nd`/`^tbkhh`/paren drops.

## Delivered (fix1 — minimal integrity patch, reworked after author review)

Author rule (review of PR #699): names are source-attested, never invented.
`Dong Nai Formosa` and `Ha Tinh Formosa` keep two same-name rows each —
distinct unit groups of one complex (operational base vs proposed expansion,
disjoint `units_included`); they are the data model, not defects.

- `data/reference/vietnam_thermal_v1_fix1.csv` (162 rows) and
  `vietnam_thermal_units_v1_fix1.csv` (249 rows), built reproducibly from the
  frozen v1 by `experiments/scripts/build_reference_v1_fix1.py` (verbatim text
  transform — a spreadsheet round-trip had coerced `ires_code` 0121->121).
- Two defects fixed: DH2 romanization dup deleted (both levels);
  `Quảng Trị 1` "Unit 2, Unit 2" transcription error -> Units 1+2 (both
  levels; upstream unit master is sound — root cause is the aggregator, 0416).
- `tests/test_reference_integrity.py` (red on v1, green on fix1): unit names
  fold-unique; same-name plant rows pairwise status-distinct with disjoint
  `units_included`; 4-digit `ires_code` guard; no repeated unit in a row.
- `PROVENANCE.md` fix1 entry; `fp_audit_exp2.py` gains `--reference/--label`.

## Measured non-finding (audit before instrumenting)

Re-reconciling all 80 Exp2 runs: FP 399->399; FN 7617->7537 (the delta is
phantom misses of the deleted duplicate row; DNF/HTF FN merely relabel —
models rarely report those plants at all). The 14 remaining `clean_name`
collisions cause neither FP nor FN. FP is dominated by `matcher_fail_lp_veto`
(201 occ -> 0393) and `reference_hole` (99 occ -> 0395). Therefore the
cleaner gate and `name_ascii` alias are deliberately NOT implemented — no
over-fitting the cleaner to the Vietnam instance.

## Exit criteria (rescoped)

- [x] All 17 collision groups adjudicated by the author (1 dup deleted +
      1 typo fixed; DNF/HTF legitimate same-name rows; 14 documented
      non-finding)
- [x] fix1 files built reproducibly; untouched fields byte-identical;
      no invented names
- [x] `tests/test_reference_integrity.py` green on fix1, red on v1
- [x] `PROVENANCE.md` version entry
- [x] FP/FN deltas measured on existing outputs and explained
- Descoped: `name_ascii`, cleaner gate, Makefile wiring and adoption
  (follow-up ticket; Makefile redesign 0406 in flight — do not touch)

## Related

- `data/reference/PROVENANCE.md` §fix1 — canonical record of the edits
- 0392/0393 (matcher — FP levers), 0395 (reference holes; unblocked by this)
- Follow-up tickets: archive Cergy communication (release/tag/HAL/page perso);
  adopt fix1 (before/after figures, then rewire)
